TITLE: Dynamic grouping instead of enforced tiers

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-PLAN-GRAMMAR-RESHAPE
TITLE: Dynamic grouping instead of enforced tiers
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Reshape how plans are expressed. The operator's direction, needing more
unpacking in a future session (their words): kill enforced epic/story/task
TIERS -- "epics of epics of epics of stories of stories just become dynamic
levels" for grouping how they reason over an execution plan -- but keep a
way to mark a CLUSTER versus a detailed task list (maybe just a boolean
field) so a kanban view and a tree view can each cut the same plan. Order
should respect dependency order; grouping exists because nobody can reason
over the whole tree at once.

The use cases they separated, realizing they are managing several
representations with different goals in one system:
- complexity depth: work breakdown -- story/task-like, nesting allowed, a
  tight coupling of dependencies among nodes;
- details depth: how much specificity the HUMAN pins before the LLM may
  elect the rest -- the degrees of freedom allowed in implementation
  (pre-beads);
- organization: epic-like higher-level reasoning;
- axes, as their own node kind or as fields: milestone = horizontal slice
  over time, named component = vertical slice -- shaped like nodes/relations
  so prose can attach to them.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator: "yeah this one needs more unpacking in future session" and
"pretty much describing the status quo, lol, but no enforced tier levels."
Axes clause verbatim, since node-kind-vs-field is theirs to pick: "various
axis (own node kind or fields?). horizontal slice over time: milestone.
verticle slice of like named components. kinda like node / relations so I
can attach prose to those."
<<<
